! mcp_bootstrap_p265.strap -- MCP printed page 265: JOB CONTROL PHASE 1
! OVERLAPPED, its opening (YJC1TT DD .. NOP), lines 1-49.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.16, read at 400 dpi, doubtful glyphs
! at 900 dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD
! ID PE000001  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 265" (round glyphs in
! numeric fields read 0).  The heading row's LOCATION field is BLANK.
! A NEW CARD DECK: p.264 is the PD deck; this page's serials start at
! PE000001.
!
! THE PAGE.  49 lines; every line number prints a "*" after it.  Lines
! 1-3 and 10-12 are remark cards (banner), line 4 CNOP prints no
! location (230747.00 already a word: emits nothing), line 7 EXT(0,18)
! prints no location.  Located rows run contiguous from 230747.00 to
! 230777.40 (a half word; next location 231000.00), then blank paper.
! "*" after the LOCATION on lines 6, 9 and 30.
!   line 5   YJC1TT DD(BU,12),(8)0401 prints "04C1" = 0401 (12 bits).
!   line 6   DR(BU,33),(1) at 230747.14 prints 000000.41 (the size,
!            33 bits; DR rows get no !CHECK).
!   lines 7-8 EXT(0,18) over B,YC11ST: prints 0461724 at 230747.55 =
!            the 19-bit half-word address of YC11ST (230752.00).
!   line 9   DR(BU),(2) at 230750.00 prints 000002.00 (two words).
! JOIN.  p.264 (PD deck, not landed, no neighbour deck) -- contiguity
! with it is NOT established here: this page opens on a CNOP whose
! row prints no location.  p.121's landed deck SYNs YJC1TT at
! (8)230747.00, which this page's line 5 defines there -- an
! independent witness of the origin.  p.266 should open at 231000.00
! with serial PE000049.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * YC11ST (label line 13, operand line 8): both glyphs after C print
!     the flagged 1 at 900 dpi (the unflagged I of YISUKM, LVI differs);
!     the volume OCR also reads YC11ST.  EXT/B prints 0461724 = 230752.0.
!   * line 28 ",SKCM" = ,SKOM (open O): landed p.106 "S KOM SYN,79.32";
!     prints 000117.40.
!   * line 29 ",3.C" = ,3.0; line 35 "XW,C" = XW,0; line 41 "BR,C($14)"
!     = BR,0($14): open round glyphs, digits by context; binaries agree.
!   * line 40 prints "LV,$14,Y1UCXW +1.0" WITH a blank before "+"; the
!     binary 230771.34 includes the +1.0, so the blank is inside the
!     operand (STRAP drops blanks in an operand).  Written as printed.
!   * hex bytes printed with an open round written 0 ("C1" lines 33,
!     46 = 01; "FC" line 24 = F0 as line 26's CM0000 prints F0); octal fields "CCCCCC.CC" are 0.
!
! EXTERNALS.  Values for symbols defined on pages not landed come from
! this page's binary.  Where the volume OCR (a finding aid only) shows
! the defining card's operation, the SYN carries that dds:
!   YC1MTT  DD(BU,12)  (OCR "YCIMTT DD(BU,12),(8)0401")
!   YSPDCR  C-I        half-word instruction (BU,32,8)
!   YC1TC   BB         full-word instruction (BU,64,8)
!   YC1B    L(BU,12)   full-word instruction (BU,64,8)
!   YC1JJC  VF,0       plain
!   YC1C, YC1JC, YC1DB, YUNCOD, YISUKM, LASTPP: defining card not seen;
!   plain SYN.  (LASTPP and YUNCOD carry other values in the IPL
!   assembly pp.15-98 -- p.57 "LASTPP SYN,(8)2613.0", p.25 "YUNCOD
!   SYN,(8)2166.0" -- a different assembly; the body's values are
!   these.)
!
! CARD SERIALS.  PE000001 .. PE000048; lines 7-8 (the EXT pair) share
! PE000007, so line N prints PE00000N through line 7 and PE0000(N-1)
! from line 8.  None skipped.

SREJJB  SYN, (8)215011.40            ! landed p.103 "S REJJB VF,0" at 215011.40; LV line 13 215011.74
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0             ! landed p.103 label (as p.128/p.142/p.153)
